    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0279" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/359</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Advisory Commission of Railway
                        Experts to Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-10T11:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10, 1918,
                                11 a.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11.47 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>After a month exasperating unnecessary delays have succeeded getting arrangements
                    for placing units to cover all the Chinese Eastern Railway at once, and hope a
                    little later Vladivostok. No trains operating between Manchuria, Chita. Line
                    held by strong force reported Bolsheviki, Germans, Austrians.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
